Z||000000||Hank is Here||11-30-2000||07:25 PM||||Okay<BR>from what I understand there are different PROM's depending on engine and tranny configuration.  What if you were to place a 5 speed in a 4 speed car and did not change the PROM, any performance differences?<BR>Also on auto's what about going to a true o/d tranny what PROM would you use or stick with teh stock 3 speed one?<P>Lastly where are the PROM's located in the car, what do they look like?<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jackalrr||11-30-2000||07:45 PM||||I too am interested in the answer to this question. I have an 85 GT that had the 4 speed replaced with a 5. I think the PROM is on the computer, but I'm not sure.<P><BR>-Charlie<BR>------<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-30-2000||07:46 PM||||The PROM is in the ECM. Exactly what it looks like depends which ECM is involved.<P>The diferances tranny wise are mostly subtle things. It's posible you could set bogus codes under some conditions. I've never heard of it happening but it's possible so it's something to keep in mind.<P>Just how much diferance it makes form 4 speed to 5 speed stick depends partly on just what tranny gearing is involved. Usually it's not a very big deal. You should be able to find the right PROM for most Fiero combinations.<P>The automatic is the same way. depends partly on the gearing. There are no AOD PROMs for Fiero but it's posible an AOD PROM would work from another GM car. The posibility of that depends on just which ECM is involved. <P>Again tho I've heard no specific problems caused by chagning the tranny. Remember these ECM's don't control anything in the tranny but the torque converter lock in the automatic. It's not like the newer PCM's that control the engine and all the tranny functions.<P><B>WARNING</B> PROMs are ECM model specific. You can't take a PROM from one type ECM and use it in another.<P>there are some more notes that may help in my cave. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-30-2000||08:56 PM||||How much detail do you want? <P>The same ECM part number can use several different layouts and program code. For example, the Syclone/Typhoon, Sunbird GT Turbo and Quad 4 (for certain years) used the same ECM 1227749. The Quad 4 code was totally different while the Syclone/Typhoon/Sunbird were the same. Only the calibrations were different due to engine size.<P>On the otherhand, it is possible to run one ECM's code in another's since many are very similar in hardware. Some have extra parts load, some have parts missing. The 9396 and 7727 are like that. More RAM in the 9396. The 7730 and 7727 are identical other than case. The problem is figuring out the differences. The 85 X-11 is the same hardware as the Fiero V6, but different internal program code. <P>Finally, if the engine is the same and the ECM is the same, it is likely that the code will be the same although the cars might be different (eg, the 85 Camaro vs the 85 Citation V6). Fan turn on temps, TCC stuff might be a bit different.<P>If you are talking only about the Fiero 4 spd vs 5 spd, the chips are interchangeable, but the shift lights will be turned on in the wrong places. Otherwise, it will work. The gear ratio's are different so the RPM/MPH will be different (which is how it tells what gear it's in) so it will turn the light on in the wrong places.<P>If you are hoping for more power, it's unlikely to be found by using another car's chip unless it is so wrong it goes into backup or runs the thing so lean you'll burn it up. Don't try that.<P>More detail?<P>Terry<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-30-2000||09:14 PM||||In this case I was staying mostly to the Fiero ECM's but you had stuff in there I hadn't even got to for the stick. (I have an automatic so I don't pay much attention to stick.)<P>It also depends what year/motor fiero. If you have a DIS 4 cyl motor that 1227748 ECM is easier to find alternate PROMs for but you have to know how they work. <P>The 1227748 ECM and the cast iron 2.5l DIS motor are used in a bunch of GM cars. The PROMs from those cars won't all work in the Fiero. Why? not becuase of the motor or tranny but because of how the VSS talks to the ECM. The VSS input source is selected in the PROM. (You can feed it in directly or thru the buffer like Fiero does.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||11-30-2000||10:06 PM||||Some of the 2.5L cars do gen the ECM VSS from the speedo (even with a cable), but you're right. It's a hit and miss without some research. A car's come to mind.||||reg||1
